        {
            "id": "f161204f-7185-4846-993a-4470e3cb3f44",
            "build_id": "ae90c06a-17a6-4d38-bac2-a5f6c141418c",
            "round_number": 3,
            "cash_earned": 0,
            "created_at": "2025-10-02T03:50:43.638997+00:00",
            "notes": "I prefer to take [Protective Beam](item_3f1ef995-8ecc-45fb-8b57-26fdccc21feb) before [Distortion](item_5557e2f2-02df-4eac-8128-0c23b71183b1) because unlike the latter, Protective Beam's benefit is applied regardless of whether your beam target is dealing damage, and helps mitigate riskier angles and plays. It also helps your beam stay connected longer, letting your take stealthier angles.\n\nIf you're getting hard targeted, take [Serenity](item_c6e1c072-ff50-467e-b59f-9506baea10c1).\n\nThe blue/green items for weapon power and speed can be mixed and matched depending on what you can afford.  [Advanced Nanobiotics](item_26fcf7c9-b81a-4d8e-a459-b515519cb73e) + [Talon Modification Module](item_c0ca1795-a3ea-4dc9-ae17-f34122574b3a) is the ideal blue item combo at this stage, but if you can't afford it or need to prioritize surviving with [Vital-E-Tee](item_b92e6f1d-3aac-4eec-b027-00c8e1529016), aim for a mix of weapon power and weapon speed (taking into account [Advanced Nanobiotics](item_26fcf7c9-b81a-4d8e-a459-b515519cb73e)'s near constantly proc'd weapon speed boost that won't be reflected in your stats), since they stack multiplicatively.\n\nIn other words, 10 WP + 10 WS will output more healing than 20 WP + 0 WS.",
